00:35:17.740 --> 00:35:21.310
So the question of the week is,
how do I describe my Java app?

00:35:21.310 --> 00:35:23.410
So I've used plenty
of Docker files,

00:35:23.410 --> 00:35:25.060
but it's usually
copied and pasted

00:35:25.060 --> 00:35:27.400
from the base template, and
then slight modifications.

00:35:27.400 --> 00:35:29.920
They can get pretty complex
and pretty unwieldy.

00:35:29.920 --> 00:35:31.900
So the answer to
this question is JIB.

00:35:31.900 --> 00:35:33.730
And JIB is built to
kind of integrate

00:35:33.730 --> 00:35:35.950
with your current Java
development workflow,

00:35:35.950 --> 00:35:39.280
and help you build your
Docker files without needing

00:35:39.280 --> 00:35:42.170
to kind of get into
the complexity of them.

00:35:42.170 --> 00:35:44.670
So the idea is that you
basically just kind of put it

00:35:44.670 --> 00:35:45.700
in the configuration.

00:35:45.700 --> 00:35:48.370
If you're using Maven or
Gradle, it's pretty simple,

00:35:48.370 --> 00:35:50.120
or you can just
use it by itself.

00:35:50.120 --> 00:35:52.060
And then you just
point to a place

00:35:52.060 --> 00:35:54.260
to host your actual Docker file.

00:35:54.260 --> 00:35:55.730
And from there,
you're good to go.

00:35:55.730 --> 00:35:57.190
It's really, really
simple to set up,

00:35:57.190 --> 00:35:58.857
and actually, there's
a fun little video

00:35:58.857 --> 00:36:01.658
that just got published that
shows you how to use it,

00:36:01.658 --> 00:36:03.700
and then links over to
the official documentation

00:36:03.700 --> 00:36:05.270
so you go check that out.

00:36:05.270 --> 00:36:06.700
But it's a pretty
simple process,

00:36:06.700 --> 00:36:09.810
and I think it's really valuable
for being able to containerize

00:36:09.810 --> 00:36:12.572
and deploy your Java
application without having

00:36:12.572 --> 00:36:14.530
to worry about what's
going on-- without having

00:36:14.530 --> 00:36:16.760
to worry about all the
configuration management.

00:36:16.760 --> 00:36:20.230
It's just so much more easy
to put together a Docker file

00:36:20.230 --> 00:36:22.900
based on what your Java app
is, and then move along--

00:36:22.900 --> 00:36:25.480
focus on the actual part that
matters, which is your code.

00:36:25.480 --> 00:36:27.610
So check out the video,
definitely check out

00:36:27.610 --> 00:36:28.948
GIB on GitHub.

00:36:28.948 --> 00:36:30.490
And then if it's
interesting, give it

00:36:30.490 --> 00:36:31.960
a shot-- see what
you can do with it,

00:36:31.960 --> 00:36:34.043
and see how it can kind
of make that whole process

00:36:34.043 --> 00:36:34.628
a lot easier.

